WEBVTT

00:01.720 --> 00:03.230
Now that's adorable!

00:03.230 --> 00:05.040
I'll upload a story.

00:10.640 --> 00:13.070
Ooh, I'm lookin' good.

00:17.520 --> 00:19.080
What are you looking at?

00:20.310 --> 00:23.480
In the ear?! 
Don't sneak up on me like that!

00:24.530 --> 00:28.050
Whoa, brings me back! The winter festival!

00:28.540 --> 00:31.160
What, Tsubasa, are you interested?

00:31.480 --> 00:35.350
It's this weekend, so I thought 
it might be worth checking out.

00:36.290 --> 00:37.810
This weekend...

00:38.990 --> 00:41.540
Well all right, Tsubasa.

00:41.540 --> 00:42.420
Huh?

00:42.420 --> 00:46.360
If you're going to insist, 
then I guess I could go with you.

00:46.630 --> 00:48.530
Did I even say that though?

00:51.570 --> 00:52.760
Does that mean...

00:53.300 --> 00:55.030
<i>A date?!</i>

01:07.080 --> 01:09.750
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are Super Adorable!</b>

01:10.590 --> 01:13.960
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are Super Adorable!</b>

02:22.120 --> 02:24.970
Super Cute Angels ♥

02:22.120 --> 02:24.970
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are</b>

02:22.120 --> 02:24.970
<b>Boom!</b>

02:22.120 --> 02:24.970
<b>Super Adorable</b>

02:30.410 --> 02:31.670
Yummy!

02:31.830 --> 02:36.670
<b>Episode 2
It's Super Warm Inside the Snow Fort</b>

02:31.830 --> 02:36.670
<b>Episode 2:
It's Super Warm Inside the Snow Fort</b>

02:32.030 --> 02:33.820
I love this mochi!

02:33.820 --> 02:36.680
The sweet potato mochi? 
The other one has cheese.

02:36.680 --> 02:39.510
Yay! Cheesy, cheesy!

02:41.390 --> 02:45.860
<b>Soft
Katsugen</b>

02:41.570 --> 02:43.020
And your Katsugen.

02:43.020 --> 02:44.250
Thank ya.

02:47.010 --> 02:48.760
Papa's late.

02:48.760 --> 02:50.770
Well, it is the weekend.

02:51.120 --> 02:54.990
But tomorrow is a day off. 
Should we all go somewhere?

02:54.990 --> 02:56.530
I wanna go skating!

02:56.530 --> 02:59.550
Okay, okay! You coming, Mii?

03:03.210 --> 03:04.690
I gotta pass.

03:04.690 --> 03:07.250
I'm going to the winter festival 
with a friend tomorrow.

03:07.250 --> 03:10.640
Aww, aren't you coming tomorrow, Big Mii?

03:10.640 --> 03:11.940
Sorry, Momo.

03:11.940 --> 03:16.930
Winter festival, huh? You always used 
to go in elementary school, Mii.

03:18.930 --> 03:21.320
Mio-chan said they were gonna go, too.

03:21.860 --> 03:23.050
I'm back!

03:23.660 --> 03:25.730
Welcome home!

03:28.190 --> 03:31.190
Kitami Winter Festival

03:28.190 --> 03:31.190
<b>The Kitami Winter Festival will be held in early February with the theme"Snow
Is Our Friend." In this festival, snow statues, ice sculptures, a large snow slide,
...and stage events will be held, so enjoy the winter...</b>

03:37.400 --> 03:39.730
Today's another cold one.

03:40.870 --> 03:45.370
Looking forward to it!

03:40.870 --> 03:45.370
Meet me in front of
Kitami Station at 11:00 tomorrow.
'Kay, good night

03:40.870 --> 03:45.370
Yeah. Good night

03:41.150 --> 03:45.850
<i>Meet me in front of Kitami Station 
at 11:00 tomorrow. 'Kay, good night!</i>

03:45.850 --> 03:49.230
<i>I can't believe we're 
actually going together.</i>

03:49.230 --> 03:53.110
<i>Going to the festival together... 
Isn't this totally a date?</i>

03:53.110 --> 03:57.000
I mean, she even added 
that emoji! And then this?

04:00.610 --> 04:05.160
<i>I can't! If I get this hyped before we 
even meet, I'll never make it back alive!</i>

04:05.720 --> 04:10.190
<i>Okay, I'll have to focus on just
enjoying my first Hokkaido event.</i>

04:10.890 --> 04:12.610
<i>As for Fuyuki-san,</i>

04:12.610 --> 04:15.250
<b>Please Press</b>

04:13.120 --> 04:17.560
<i>maybe she invited me just to be nice, 
since I don't have any friends.</i>

04:15.250 --> 04:16.690
<b>Please Wait</b>

04:20.110 --> 04:23.120
<b>Kitami Station</b>

04:24.050 --> 04:25.970
Thanks for waiting, Tsubasa!

04:36.430 --> 04:37.600
Hiya.

04:37.600 --> 04:39.970
<i>What a powerful attack!</i>

04:39.970 --> 04:43.700
So, Fuyuki-san, are those 
your normal street clothes?

04:43.700 --> 04:46.930
<i>She's usually so casual, 
the lack of skin now is even sexier!</i>

04:46.930 --> 04:50.890
Oh, that's right. This is the first 
time we've gone out on a day off.

04:51.500 --> 04:52.730
Pretty cute, huh?

04:54.800 --> 04:56.880
Yes. Very.

04:57.500 --> 05:01.570
Hey, you sound like I made 
you say it! Not nice.

05:02.590 --> 05:07.820
S-So, Fuyuki-san, you haven't gone to a 
winter festival since elementary school, right?

05:07.820 --> 05:10.500
That's right. Been a super long time.

05:10.720 --> 05:14.020
They're going to have snow statues 
and ice sculptures, right?

05:14.020 --> 05:16.500
Stuff you can only see in Hokkaido.

05:16.500 --> 05:19.850
I also looked up the local 
specialties at the food stands.

05:20.260 --> 05:21.990
This is gonna be fun!

05:21.990 --> 05:25.140
Maybe you shouldn't get your hopes up.

05:25.140 --> 05:27.290
Hmm? Did you say something?

05:27.290 --> 05:30.100
Nothin'! M'kay, let's go.

05:30.100 --> 05:31.410
Oh. Yeah!

05:38.570 --> 05:41.490
Kitami Winter Festival

05:40.450 --> 05:42.130
Whoa.

05:41.490 --> 05:43.990
<b><b>Buttered Potatoes</b></b>

05:41.490 --> 05:43.990
<b><b>Yakisoba</b></b>

05:52.370 --> 05:54.560
This is basically it, so if—

05:55.270 --> 05:56.990
This is great, Fuyuki-san!

05:56.990 --> 05:58.380
Let's go look!

05:59.870 --> 06:01.470
Okay!

06:05.490 --> 06:07.160
The snow sculptures are huge!

06:07.160 --> 06:09.450
I think they used to be bigger.

06:09.450 --> 06:11.650
Or maybe you just grew up.

06:11.650 --> 06:13.070
Time for a picture.

06:13.070 --> 06:15.310
Good idea! Even better

06:16.000 --> 06:18.110
if we do it this way!

06:18.110 --> 06:18.860
Huh?! Wait—!

06:20.360 --> 06:23.270
<i>Wow. She smells so good!</i>

06:24.170 --> 06:28.820
Oh. Your eyes are half closed, Tsubasa. 
Hilarious!

06:28.820 --> 06:32.580
Wha-?! That's embarrassing! Delete it!

06:32.580 --> 06:33.790
What's that smell?

06:33.790 --> 06:35.340
Are you even listening?

06:35.670 --> 06:37.450
Tsubasa, are you hungry?

06:37.450 --> 06:40.130
Huh? I guess.

06:40.130 --> 06:43.130
Corn Dogs

06:43.130 --> 06:44.600
What do you want on it?

06:44.600 --> 06:45.720
Sugar!

06:45.720 --> 06:46.550
Me, too.

06:46.550 --> 06:48.550
<b>Corn Dogs</b>

06:46.550 --> 06:48.550
<b>Ketchup</b>

06:46.550 --> 06:48.550
<b>Pepper</b>

06:46.550 --> 06:48.550
<b>Sugar</b>

06:50.640 --> 06:52.970
O-One corn dog.

06:52.970 --> 06:55.020
Comin' up! What do you want on it?

06:56.010 --> 06:57.520
Sugar.

06:59.550 --> 07:01.990
Yakitori ish sho good!

07:02.410 --> 07:04.530
What should I eat next?

07:04.530 --> 07:06.300
Sorry to keep you waiting.

07:06.300 --> 07:07.530
Welcome back!

07:07.750 --> 07:08.570
Oh.

07:12.300 --> 07:15.830
Hey, can I have a bite 
of your corn dog, Tsubasa?

07:15.830 --> 07:17.680
Huh? Yeah, sure.

07:28.120 --> 07:30.930
Ooh, yummy!

07:31.690 --> 07:32.850
Good to hear.

07:33.070 --> 07:35.920
<i>Why did that feel so dirty?</i>

07:35.920 --> 07:40.160
<i>And I have to finish it 
after she took a bite?</i>

07:40.160 --> 07:41.220
<i>Isn't that an...</i>

07:42.070 --> 07:43.540
<i>indirect ki—!</i>

07:44.650 --> 07:47.940
<i>No, don't think about it! 
You're in high school, man!</i>

07:47.940 --> 07:50.020
<i>Just eat it like normal.</i>

07:51.930 --> 07:54.120
<i>All right, I did it!</i>

07:56.680 --> 07:58.370
Uh, what is it?

07:58.370 --> 08:00.520
Nah, it's nothing.

08:00.520 --> 08:04.140
I just wish everyone was as 
easy to read as you, Tsubasa.

08:04.640 --> 08:06.420
You're totally making fun of me!

08:06.420 --> 08:08.220
'Kay, let's keep going!

08:08.220 --> 08:10.720
Uh, wait, Fuyuki-san!

08:23.970 --> 08:24.730
Here.

08:25.230 --> 08:27.360
They were passing out hot amazake.

08:27.690 --> 08:28.950
Thank ya.

08:30.090 --> 08:31.540
Enjoying the festival?

08:31.850 --> 08:34.480
All this snow and ice is just... wow!

08:34.480 --> 08:37.160
You're at a loss for words! Hilarious!

08:40.880 --> 08:44.880
I've only lived in Tokyo, 
so I really feel it.

08:46.010 --> 08:50.240
This is still Japan, 
but the landscape is so different.

08:49.170 --> 08:51.590
<b>Kitami</b>

08:53.370 --> 08:56.100
Thank you for today! It was so much fun!

08:56.540 --> 08:58.510
I'm so glad you came with me, Fuyuki-san!

09:06.590 --> 09:09.490
I was actually a little worried about today.

09:09.490 --> 09:10.900
Huh? Why?

09:11.150 --> 09:16.520
Well, the last time I came to the festival, 
I was still in elementary school.

09:16.520 --> 09:20.250
I had fun back then, but I didn't 
know if it would still be fun now.

09:20.970 --> 09:24.890
I was worried you'd be disappointed 
and think, "what, is that it?"

09:27.910 --> 09:31.300
But it turns out I didn't 
need to worry at all!

09:31.660 --> 09:36.830
When I'm with you, Tsubasa, 
you make me like Hokkaido even more!

09:37.340 --> 09:40.200
I remember how nice this town really is!

09:40.900 --> 09:44.640
And when I see you having fun, 
it kinda makes me feel happy!

09:44.640 --> 09:47.590
I'm glad I came to the festival with you, too!

09:50.850 --> 09:56.620
I never realized it before, 
but I might actually love my home town.

09:57.640 --> 09:58.790
Ah... Huh?

10:00.100 --> 10:00.910
Watch out!

10:15.920 --> 10:19.160
Ah, um... I-I-I'm Sorry!

10:19.160 --> 10:21.460
I just, yeah, um...

10:21.460 --> 10:23.770
I... I'm fine.

10:24.790 --> 10:26.100
Thank ya.

10:30.560 --> 10:31.770
Fuyuki-san?

10:31.770 --> 10:32.780
Hmm?

10:33.060 --> 10:37.950
Maybe, if you're okay with it, 
we can go out again somewhere together?

10:42.930 --> 10:47.170
Heh? What's this now? Are you that 
desperate to hang out with me again?

10:47.170 --> 10:52.590
<b>Pedestrians & Bicycles
Only</b>

10:47.370 --> 10:51.500
W-Well, it doesn't have 
to be just the two of us.

10:52.950 --> 10:56.370
I want to go to the Sapporo 
Snow Festival someday, too.

10:57.790 --> 10:58.550
Yeah.

11:11.480 --> 11:12.070
Whoa!

11:12.500 --> 11:14.560
Let's eat lunch together!

11:15.700 --> 11:19.470
I brought something I want you to try today.

11:19.470 --> 11:20.160
Me?

11:20.160 --> 11:22.410
<b>Only Available in Hokkaido</b>

11:20.160 --> 11:22.410
<b>Always Delicious!!</b>

11:20.420 --> 11:21.750
Ta-da!

11:22.410 --> 11:25.050
Huh? What is it, cup noodles?

11:25.050 --> 11:28.330
Whenever I eat cup noodles at school,

11:28.330 --> 11:30.230
Open To Here

11:28.330 --> 11:31.070
they always taste so much better than normal.

11:32.040 --> 11:35.060
I bet you don't see a lot 
of yakiben in Tokyo, right?

11:35.060 --> 11:39.200
Huh? Wait, did you go and 
buy this just for me?

11:39.200 --> 11:41.870
When I saw your reaction the other day,

11:41.140 --> 11:42.600
<b>Salt-Grilled
Scallops</b>

11:41.870 --> 11:45.100
it made me want to introduce 
you to more Hokkaido cuisine!

11:46.570 --> 11:48.980
<i>I can't describe how embarrassing this is!</i>

11:49.390 --> 11:52.410
Oh, you brought hot water in a bottle?

11:52.410 --> 11:55.240
Yup, yup! Now we just wait three minutes.

11:55.000 --> 11:57.610
3 Minutes Later

11:55.790 --> 11:57.610
Yeah, all done!

11:57.840 --> 12:00.160
It sure doesn't take long.

12:00.160 --> 12:02.180
Now here's the trick.

12:02.520 --> 12:03.030
Huh?

12:03.480 --> 12:07.330
Yakiben come with Chinese soup broth

12:03.570 --> 12:07.330
<b>Furikake</b>

12:03.570 --> 12:07.330
<b>Chinese Soup</b>

12:07.700 --> 12:11.310
so you can make soup with 
the water you pour out!

12:11.310 --> 12:13.840
Huh. That's a neat idea.

12:14.100 --> 12:16.260
Finished!

12:16.650 --> 12:18.800
<i>This looks like total junk food!</i>

12:18.800 --> 12:24.020
<i>Nevertheless, it tempts my appetite with 
its powerful appearance and fragrance!</i>

12:27.070 --> 12:28.850
Here. Say "aah."

12:29.160 --> 12:29.850
Yumph—!

12:30.110 --> 12:31.730
<i>"Say aah" already?!</i>

12:35.650 --> 12:36.680
Taste okay?

12:38.640 --> 12:40.450
It's really good!

12:40.450 --> 12:42.530
Right? I'm glad.

12:42.530 --> 12:44.670
The noodles are nice and firm

12:44.670 --> 12:46.690
and the cabbage and other 
ingredients are covered in sauce.

12:46.690 --> 12:48.190
It's really good!

12:49.920 --> 12:52.460
So now I've gotten you back 
for the winter festival.

12:52.460 --> 12:54.710
<i>Oh, she means that time...</i>

12:56.180 --> 12:59.200
Hey, Tsubasa. You're blushing, you know.

12:59.200 --> 13:01.050
Did you get turned on just thinking about it?

13:01.050 --> 13:04.010
No! It's 'cause the yakisoba is so hot!

13:04.010 --> 13:06.000
So wait, what's in your bento?

13:06.000 --> 13:07.790
I wanna see! Show me!

13:07.790 --> 13:10.190
It's just a normal bento.

13:10.530 --> 13:11.900
Like this.

13:13.800 --> 13:16.820
Normal... for New Year's?

13:17.030 --> 13:19.360
This is sick! Can I take a picture?

13:19.360 --> 13:20.510
Yeah, I guess.

13:20.510 --> 13:23.820
<i>Is my bento really that unusual?</i>

13:23.820 --> 13:25.310
Do you want to try some, Fuyuki-san?

13:25.310 --> 13:28.250
Huh? Is that okay? I do, I do!

13:28.750 --> 13:31.670
I'll try the meat, then. Thank you!

13:34.600 --> 13:36.920
It's super yummy!

13:36.920 --> 13:40.250
What even is this meat? 
It's so juicy and tender!

13:40.250 --> 13:43.360
Who even made it? God? 
Is this God meat?

13:43.360 --> 13:46.400
It's stewed pork that my grandma made.

13:46.400 --> 13:50.850
Huh? That's crazy! 
I think I wanna marry your granny!

13:50.850 --> 13:51.980
What do you mean?!

13:52.850 --> 13:56.730
Whew! That was totally amay-and-zing. Thanks!

13:56.960 --> 14:01.400
And thank you for the yakisoba bento. 
It was delicious.

14:01.890 --> 14:06.740
I had never eaten cup noodles in my 
life, but they really were delicious!

14:06.740 --> 14:09.490
Everything is a new experience 
with you, Fuyuki-san.

14:09.890 --> 14:10.700
Hmm?

14:10.700 --> 14:13.880
Did you just say you'd never 
eaten cup noodles before?

14:13.880 --> 14:14.670
Huh? Yeah.

14:14.670 --> 14:19.380
U-Uh, h-hold on a minute. And then what? 
Everything is a new experience?

14:19.810 --> 14:21.050
Yeah, uh...

14:21.050 --> 14:26.620
L-Like my first time going to a girl's 
house or shopping at a convenience store.

14:27.140 --> 14:31.020
Also, I'd never gone to a 
festival with a friend before.

14:32.060 --> 14:33.270
Really?

14:33.270 --> 14:34.060
Yeah.

14:34.060 --> 14:38.950
With what you're saying now, and with that 
bento... Tsubasa, does that mean you're...

14:39.440 --> 14:41.970
a really spoiled rich kid?

14:41.970 --> 14:42.690
Huh?

14:42.690 --> 14:46.180
I could tell your aura or 
something was different from us.

14:46.180 --> 14:48.780
Yeah, totally like someone from Tokyo!

14:48.780 --> 14:52.500
I think you have the wrong 
idea about Tokyo, Fuyuki-san.

14:52.500 --> 14:56.270
And I don't think my family 
is very rich at all.

14:56.270 --> 15:00.800
Huh? You've got to be! 
I mean, what else would explain it?

15:01.380 --> 15:03.070
Explain...?

15:03.070 --> 15:07.220
Then hey, how about this? 
Can I come over to your place today?

15:08.470 --> 15:09.130
What?

15:13.250 --> 15:15.620
<i>She got her way after all.</i>

15:15.970 --> 15:17.310
<i>And of course she did, after that...</i>

15:17.580 --> 15:19.830
Can I come over to your place today?

15:20.780 --> 15:23.970
<i>Talk about an extremely lethal angle!</i>

15:25.640 --> 15:28.390
<i>What am I gonna do now? 
Grandma's at home.</i>

15:28.390 --> 15:30.770
Hey, Tsubasa! Come here!

15:31.660 --> 15:34.200
Look, I found a snow fort!

15:34.470 --> 15:38.470
I bet some kids built it 
and then just left it here.

15:39.910 --> 15:41.630
Fuyuki-san, um...

15:44.000 --> 15:45.700
Come inside with me.

15:52.800 --> 15:54.700
This your first time?

15:54.700 --> 15:57.640
Huh? Um, yeah, it is...

15:57.640 --> 15:58.480
Oh, god!

15:59.090 --> 16:01.400
Really warm inside, isn't it?

16:01.670 --> 16:04.890
It's s-so tight, Fuyuki-san.

16:05.500 --> 16:07.980
Hold me closer. Come on.

16:09.250 --> 16:11.480
Too tight... I gotta pull out!

16:11.480 --> 16:14.330
No, wait! You just got in!

16:14.330 --> 16:17.500
Please don't moan like that, Fuyuki-san!

16:17.760 --> 16:18.880
<i>What is happening?</i>

16:18.880 --> 16:21.560
<i>I'm not trying to make this sound so obscene!</i>

16:21.560 --> 16:22.850
Tsubasa-chan?

16:22.850 --> 16:24.420
And now I'm hearing voices?!

16:25.020 --> 16:27.420
Fuyuki-san, I should get going.

16:29.440 --> 16:30.760
Tsubasa-chan?!

16:30.760 --> 16:31.400
Eh?

16:36.770 --> 16:39.390
What in the heavens were you doing in there?

16:39.390 --> 16:41.180
<i>Grandma?!</i>

16:41.610 --> 16:43.700
Perhaps I misheard,

16:43.700 --> 16:44.720
<i>How long was she there?</i>

16:44.720 --> 16:47.870
but I thought I overheard an extremely 
inappropriate conversation.

16:47.870 --> 16:51.160
<i>The one time I'd never want to be 
heard and she caught all of it!</i>

16:51.480 --> 16:53.210
<i>I need an excuse, fast!</i>

16:53.770 --> 16:55.240
Grandma, this isn—

16:55.240 --> 16:57.750
Aww! Tsubasa, you were way too quick!

16:58.310 --> 17:00.960
You should've enjoyed your first time more.

17:00.960 --> 17:02.080
Aah!

17:02.080 --> 17:03.210
Eek!

17:04.310 --> 17:07.080
Oh, do you know this lady?

17:07.640 --> 17:08.500
Uh...

17:09.500 --> 17:12.970
What?! Tsubasa's actual granny?!

17:12.970 --> 17:15.850
Nice to meet you! My name is Fuyuki.

17:15.850 --> 17:18.790
I never thought I'd encount you here!

17:18.790 --> 17:19.640
Enka?

17:18.910 --> 17:19.910
<b>Enka</b>

17:19.640 --> 17:24.730
Oh, by the way, I had a bit of the 
bento you made for Tsubasa, Granny.

17:25.350 --> 17:28.740
Huh? <i>You</i> tasted my cooking?

17:29.650 --> 17:30.900
Stop there, Fuyuki-san!

17:30.900 --> 17:33.360
It was super delish!

17:33.360 --> 17:35.660
Really! Like, oh my god!

17:37.040 --> 17:41.350
I'm so jealous that Tsubasa gets to 
eat homemade meals like that every day!

17:41.350 --> 17:43.170
I want to eat it again!

17:43.370 --> 17:44.900
Oh, boy.

17:46.160 --> 17:49.030
Thank you for such a lovely compliment.

17:49.030 --> 17:54.220
By the way, Fuyuki-san, 
what is your relationship to Tsubasa?

17:55.380 --> 17:56.010
We're fri—

17:56.010 --> 17:57.600
We're just classmates!

17:58.010 --> 17:59.810
Right, Fuyuki-san?

18:03.500 --> 18:04.810
Uh, yeah.

18:05.620 --> 18:07.070
I guess so.

18:11.200 --> 18:13.600
It seems to have started snowing.

18:14.260 --> 18:18.830
Please forgive me, Fuyuki-san, 
but since it has started snowing,

18:19.240 --> 18:23.190
and actually, Tsubasa and I have a 
very important appointment after this,

18:23.190 --> 18:25.200
so would you please excuse us?

18:25.940 --> 18:27.920
Let's move along, Tsubasa.

18:27.920 --> 18:29.200
W-Wait!

18:29.200 --> 18:30.590
I'm sorry, Fuyuki-san.

18:31.680 --> 18:32.720
Goodbye.

18:35.220 --> 18:37.260
<i>I knew it was never gonna work.</i>

18:37.850 --> 18:39.810
<i>I'm completely powerless.</i>

18:40.260 --> 18:44.230
<i>Grandma hates it when people act 
really open in relationships.</i>

18:45.040 --> 18:48.230
<i>This might be it. It might be over...</i>

18:49.010 --> 18:51.220
<i>my new life in Hokkaido.</i>

18:51.560 --> 18:53.990
No, I mean, like, wait!

18:53.990 --> 18:55.480
What? Why?

18:55.480 --> 18:58.220
Because Granny is using an umbrella!

18:58.620 --> 19:01.410
It is snowing right now, so of course I am.

19:01.410 --> 19:02.910
You shouldn't!

19:03.190 --> 19:08.340
If you slip and fall when your hands 
aren't free, you could get badly hurt!

19:08.650 --> 19:12.810
My grandma broke a bone 
like that a long time ago.

19:12.810 --> 19:13.550
Fuyuki-san...

19:13.970 --> 19:16.940
You can get rid of the snow 
by just brushing it off.

19:16.940 --> 19:17.960
Oh.

19:19.550 --> 19:21.620
Which way to your place, Tsubasa?

19:21.620 --> 19:23.700
It's that way.

19:23.700 --> 19:26.520
There's a crosswalk up ahead.

19:26.980 --> 19:31.060
It's covered in black ice today. 
It's slippery, so you shouldn't go that way.

19:31.650 --> 19:34.270
This way is safer and quicker.

19:34.680 --> 19:36.910
I can show you, so just follow me.

19:37.130 --> 19:40.010
I'll carry your things for you, Granny.

19:40.010 --> 19:41.030
Hey, wait!

19:41.030 --> 19:46.690
You make such delicious food! You should 
take care of your hands, Granny.

19:48.880 --> 19:50.440
Wait, Fuyuki-san!

19:50.440 --> 19:52.250
I'll carry the bag.

19:52.250 --> 19:53.730
Fine. Here.

19:55.150 --> 19:56.720
Are you mad about something?

19:56.720 --> 20:01.110
Not really. Why would I get mad at 
someone who's "just a classmate"?

20:01.110 --> 20:02.350
Wait, no, that was...!

20:03.360 --> 20:07.850
It's just hard for me to say in front 
of Grandma. But how do I put this...

20:08.460 --> 20:10.690
I think of you as a very important friend.

20:12.680 --> 20:16.490
Huh? What's that? 
I'm very important to you, Tsubasa?

20:16.490 --> 20:18.310
Wait, Fuyuki-san, keep it down!

20:18.310 --> 20:20.440
Huh, ain't that something?

20:18.920 --> 20:22.520
Oh, come on! This is so embarrassing!

20:23.120 --> 20:26.040
<b>Shiki</b>

20:29.970 --> 20:31.670
No way...

20:32.000 --> 20:32.950
Fuyuki-san?

20:32.950 --> 20:35.330
Huh? Oh, nah, it's okay!

20:35.330 --> 20:36.570
You have an appointment, right?

20:36.570 --> 20:38.400
M'kay, so I'll just go home.

20:38.400 --> 20:39.560
One moment, please.

20:40.290 --> 20:45.670
Thanks to your help, we arrived 
early and have some spare time.

20:45.670 --> 20:47.930
Would you like a cup of hot tea?

20:48.140 --> 20:51.350
Is that okay? Yeah!

20:52.090 --> 20:55.070
<i>I must be getting soft.</i>

20:55.890 --> 20:58.240
<i>Perhaps it's proof that I'm getting older.</i>

20:59.440 --> 21:06.090
<i>However, Tsubasa-chan did choose her. 
I'm sure Fuyuki-san is actually a lovely girl.</i>

21:06.090 --> 21:10.050
This is so messed up! 
Every shot I take is postworthy!

21:10.050 --> 21:13.040
Don't take so many pictures, Fuyuki-san!

21:13.610 --> 21:17.040
But I mean, it's just like 
I thought! You're rich!

21:17.040 --> 21:19.470
<i>Or perhaps I should keep 
an eye on her after all.</i>

21:19.470 --> 21:20.830
This one, too!

21:26.350 --> 21:28.350
Grandma!

21:29.100 --> 21:31.600
Oh, my. What is it, Tsubasa-chan?

21:31.910 --> 21:34.780
You know what? I'm gonna 
study and learn a whole bunch

21:34.780 --> 21:38.740
and get real important when I grow 
up so I can take care of all of you!

21:38.740 --> 21:43.940
Oh, my, Tsubasa-chan. You're such 
a sincere and kind young man.

21:46.810 --> 21:50.710
<i>I haven't seen Tsubasa-chan 
smile like this in a long time.</i>

21:51.450 --> 21:55.290
<i>Perhaps I should put my trust in that smile.</i>

21:55.970 --> 21:58.710
Tea is ready, you two!

21:58.710 --> 22:00.720
Okay! Thank you, Grandma!

22:00.720 --> 22:03.120
Yay! Thank you kindly!

23:33.930 --> 23:37.980
Ski Lesson Guidebook

23:35.330 --> 23:39.100
I'll pass around the guidebooks 
for next week's skiing lesson.

23:39.100 --> 23:41.980
Be sure to double-check 
your seating arrangements.

23:41.980 --> 23:43.990
Seat Map

23:41.980 --> 23:43.990
<b>Fuyuki</b>

23:41.980 --> 23:43.990
<b>Shiki</b>

23:44.420 --> 23:48.010
<i>I'm right behind 
Fuyuki-san. And next to...</i>

23:47.230 --> 23:49.320
<b>Fuyuki</b>

23:47.230 --> 23:49.320
<b>Shiki</b>

23:47.230 --> 23:49.320
<b>Akino</b>

23:48.530 --> 23:50.300
<i>Akino-san?</i>
